Falsifies `machine_discovery::acpi::verification::no_override_writes_outside_the_sixteen_legacy_irqs`.

The defect: the bound on an override's `source` field is gone, so a MADT interrupt
source override naming source 200 indexes a sixteen-entry array at 200. The field
is one byte straight out of a firmware table, and the array it indexes is a fixed
`[IsaIrqRouting; ISA_IRQ_COUNT]` on the stack of a function the x86 boot path calls
while bringing up the IO APIC.

The guard sits as one clause of a four-clause `if let` chain, which is the shape
that makes this plausible: a reader rewriting that chain as a `match` on the entry
variant has to carry the bound across by hand, and the pattern binding `source`
makes it read as though it had already been checked.

Expected to fail: the bounds check on `table[source as usize]`.

diff --git a/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi.rs b/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi.rs
--- a/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi.rs
+++ b/crates/machine_discovery/src/acpi.rs
@@ -450,7 +450,6 @@ pub fn isa_irq_table(body: &[u8]) -> [IsaIrqRouting; ISA_IRQ_COUNT] {
             flags,
         } = entry
             && bus == ISA_BUS
-            && (source as usize) < ISA_IRQ_COUNT
